From: BananaOS Duo Lite bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: pwm-fan: boost only when the fan is stopped

The quiet running duty is below the starting duty. Thermal updates and
floor writes must not repeat the starting pulse on an already powered fan.
Power-off and suspend clear enabled, preserving the next real start pulse.

--- a/drivers/hwmon/pwm-fan.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/pwm-fan.c
@@ -221,7 +221,8 @@
 			return 0;
 
 		period = state->period;
-		update = state->duty_cycle < ctx->pwm_duty_cycle_from_stopped;
+		update = !ctx->enabled &&
+			 state->duty_cycle < ctx->pwm_duty_cycle_from_stopped;
 		if (update)
 			state->duty_cycle = ctx->pwm_duty_cycle_from_stopped;
 		else
